.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFY-SYNC 1 "October 2026" "plugin-qualify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualify-sync \- qualify every plugin on the machine once, and again when its files change
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualify-sync
[\fB\-\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-\fIsetting\fR \fIvalue\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds every CLAP and LV2 plugin on the search paths and gives each new or changed one the quick
qualification: its pin, the real-time safety sweep, cost and latency, and its descriptor. A plugin whose
files hash as they did when it was qualified is skipped. The soak is not part of it, and each record says so.
.PP
Each plugin runs in processes of its own under a wall clock (\fBbudget_s\fR). One that crashes, hangs or is
refused is recorded as such, and the run goes on to the next. The pin file plugin-hostd loads as
\fBpin_file\fR is written whole after every plugin. When plugin-hostd answers on its command port, the
changed pins are also sent to it with \fBpin_set\fR; while a controller holds that port, they apply at its
next start.
.PP
A plugin that is no longer found, or whose bytes changed, leaves nothing behind: its pin, its qualification
record and the probe output beside it, and its descriptor are removed, and a running plugin-hostd is told with
\fBpin_clear\fR. Nothing is removed in a run that could not read a plugin bundle.
.PP
The last line on standard output counts the plugins: qualified, skipped, refused, crashed, hung,
unmeasured, and the seconds the run took.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-system
The directories of a system service, under /var/lib/omx.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Qualify every plugin again, recorded or not.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
The settings file (default /etc/omx/qualify.conf).
.TP
.BI \-\- "setting value"
Any setting of the file, as a flag: \fB\-\-budget\-s 30\fR for \fBbudget_s 30\fR.
\fBplugin-qualify-sync \-\-help\fR lists them with their defaults.
.SH FILES
/etc/omx/qualify.conf, /var/lib/omx/qualified.pins, /var/lib/omx/qualification, /var/lib/omx/descriptors,
/var/lib/omx/qualify-sync.json
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 the run went through, whatever the verdicts; 2 it could not run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plugin-qualify (1),
.BR plugin-hostd (1)
